56	# Apply to every page with a tag
57	To decorate every page with a tag, give the tag a `pageDecoration` in [[API/tag|tag.define]] in your [[CONFIG]]:
58	
59	```lua
60	tag.define {
61	  name = "person",
62	  pageDecoration = { icon = "user", cssClasses = { "person-page" } },
63	}
64	```
65	
66	A page’s own `pageDecoration` (from its frontmatter, or a `transform`) wins over the tag’s. When several of a page’s tags set the same field, the first tag in its `tags` wins. `cssClasses` from all of them are combined. Changing a tag’s decoration re-indexes the pages with that tag, so there is no need to run `Space: Reindex`.
